# Build context for .oss-scanner/Dockerfile (the Anthropic OSS Scanner image).
#
# BuildKit uses <Dockerfile>.dockerignore instead of the repository's root .dockerignore when
# both exist. The root one is an allowlist for the production image; the scanner needs the source
# tree (docs, charts, scripts, AGENTS.md) so an offline agent can read it. Left out: caches,
# generated output, anything machine-local or secret, editor and agent tooling (.claude, .cursor),
# and code that cannot run offline or is not shipped (Playwright E2E specs, the Storybook app in apps/storybook).

.git

# Dependencies and build output
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/dist
**/build
**/out
**/coverage
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/blob-report
**/.pnpm-store
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/next-env.d.ts
**/*vite.config.*.timestamp*

# Local environment and credentials
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
**/.envrc
**/.npmrc
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pem
**/gcp*.json
**/service-account*.json
**/*-credentials.json
g.json

# Machine-local agent state and editor files
.claude
.codex
.cursor
.vscode
.idea
.local
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log

# Generated at build time, or not useful to an offline audit
apps/web/uploads
apps/web/saml-connection
apps/web/certificates
apps/web/public/js
packages/database/generated
packages/database/.prisma-migrations
packages/database/schema-test-boolean
# Storybook's manifest stays: it is a workspace importer in the lockfile.
apps/storybook/**
!apps/storybook/package.json
apps/deployment-check/report
apps/web/playwright
